-capture-workers/linear/14036892/state.json" "file_sha256" "b368523ad4eef2f43817e1a8216e534017e2c2976c9deee9b346c75d12ec2bd8"} {"question" "q-277809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "775bf27c177020e55c870f78c963c0a325aada640a0b6dc177cb00c1f01938b8"} {"question" "q-277809" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/state.json" "file_sha256" "b368523ad4eef2f43817e1a8216e534017e2c2976c9deee9b346c75d12ec2bd8"} {"question" "q-277809" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "135"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/state.json" "file_sha256" "b368523ad4eef2f43817e1a8216e534017e2c2976c9deee9b346c75d12ec2bd8"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$10\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/state.json" "file_sha256" "b368523ad4eef2f43817e1a8216e534017e2c2976c9deee9b346c75d12ec2bd8"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1) & =10\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/state.json" "file_sha256" "b368523ad4eef2f43817e1a8216e534017e2c2976c9deee9b346c75d12ec2bd8"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "775bf27c177020e55c870f78c963c0a325aada640a0b6dc177cb00c1f01938b8"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/state.json" "file_sha256" "b368523ad4eef2f43817e1a8216e534017e2c2976c9deee9b346c75d12ec2bd8"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5\\pi "] ["math" "-\\frac{10\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "10\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/state.json" "file_sha256" "b368523ad4eef2f43817e1a8216e534017e2c2976c9deee9b346c75d12ec2bd8"} {"question" "q-117412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretati